From: Hades <15710513+hadesdevls@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Thu, 15 Oct 2026 23:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] renderer: compose the Dolby Vision luma a row past the rows
 that are read

With pl_render_params.active_rows, the composer of ETSI GS CCM 001
(libplacebo-9930) composes only the rows that are read and writes 0 in
the others. The composed luma needs no scaling, and libplacebo-9914 reads
such a plane texel by texel only where some plane of the image has a
sampler of fixed size; with the composed chroma scaled up bilinearly
(libplacebo-9940's dovi_ccm_plane_upscaler, the last rung of a
step-down) none has, and the luma is read with linear filtering at the
centres of its texels. A GPU that computes the weights in float then
takes a minute part of the next row, which at the first and the last
active rows is the composed row or 0, depending on whether rows were
left out. Measured on Mesa's software OpenGL ES (zink on lavapipe) with
the Dolby Vision renderer of Kodi at that rung: the picture drawn and
packed in one shader (the target flipped) had other bytes with and
without active_rows in the first active row of one picture of a profile
7 FEL stream, 89 to 92 bytes by one code of a chroma byte.

The luma is now composed in the row above and the row below the rows
that are read as well (the enhancement layer resampled for them too).
With it, on 8 pictures of that stream, both ways of Kodi's renderer give
the same bytes with and without active_rows at every rung of the
step-down (before: 4 drawings differed at the last rung), and the planes
handed to the caller (libplacebo-9932's dovi_ccm_planes) are the same in
the rows that are read.

License: LGPL-2.1-or-later, that of libplacebo and of the file changed,
whose notice stays as it is.
---
 src/renderer.c | 14 ++++++++++----
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+), 4 deletions(-)

diff --git a/src/renderer.c b/src/renderer.c
index 446ac67..809aa77 100644
--- a/src/renderer.c
+++ b/src/renderer.c
@@ -2411,10 +2411,16 @@ static const char *ccm_check(struct pass_state *pass, struct ccm_ctx *x)
               pass->dst_rect.y0 == 0 && pass->dst_rect.y1 == 2160 &&
               pass->dst_rect.x0 == 0 && pass->dst_rect.x1 == y->params.w;
     if (x->rows) {
-        // the luma: those rows; the chroma: the rows the scaler of the chroma
-        // reads for them (filter radius 3, an offset of up to a chroma row)
-        x->luma_rows[0] = y0;
-        x->luma_rows[1] = y1;
+        // the luma: those rows, and the row above and the row below them: a
+        // plane that needs no scaling is read with linear filtering at the
+        // centres of its texels where no plane of the image has a sampler of
+        // fixed size (libplacebo-9914: here, with the composed chroma scaled
+        // up bilinearly), and a GPU that computes the weights in float can
+        // take a part of the next row; the chroma: the rows the scaler of the
+        // chroma reads for them (filter radius 3, an offset of up to a chroma
+        // row)
+        x->luma_rows[0] = PL_MAX(y0 - 1, 0);
+        x->luma_rows[1] = PL_MIN(y1 + 1, y->params.h);
         x->chroma_rows[0] = PL_MAX(y0 / 2 - 6, 0);
         x->chroma_rows[1] = PL_MIN((y1 + 1) / 2 + 6, chh);
     }
